before:
```typescript
type IsText<T> = T extends string ? true : false;
const textCase: IsText<string> = true;
const numberCase: IsText<number> = false;
```
This selection happens during typechecking, not when values run.

```typescript
type Item<T> = T extends ReadonlyArray<infer E> ? E : T;
const numberItem: Item<number[]> = 3;
const textItem: Item<readonly string[]> = "blue";
```
E is the element type discovered from the array.

after:
This type gets the item type from either a mutable or readonly array. Other types stay unchanged.
```typescript
type Item<T> = T extends ReadonlyArray<infer E> ? E : T;
const numberItem: Item<number[]> = 3;
const textItem: Item<readonly string[]> = "blue";
```
`numberItem` must be a number. `textItem` must be text.
